      "id": "bug-001",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-03T22:30:00Z",
      "error_message": "Barcode scanner flashes multiple times during scanning and rarely returns results",
      "file": "mobile/lib/features/record/barcode_scanner_screen.dart",
      "root_cause": "_onDetect called await _controller.stop() at start of every detection and await _controller.start() on every error path. The stop()/start() cycle (1) made the camera preview visibly flash black-on-black, and (2) reset MobileScannerController's noDuplicates dedup state — so the same barcode in frame would re-detect immediately on every restart, creating a tight detect→stop→fail→start→detect loop until the user moved the camera away.",
      "fix": "Removed both _controller.stop() and _controller.start() calls in _onDetect — camera now stays running across the OFF lookup. Added application-level cooldown (_lastCode/_lastCodeAt with 3s _sameCodeCooldown) so a code that just failed cannot re-trigger immediately. _busy guard alone now prevents re-entrancy.",
      "tags": [
        "barcode",
        "mobile_scanner",
        "flutter",
        "camera",
        "detection-loop",
        "race-condition"
      ],
      "related_bugs": [],
